## Directory map: what belongs where

- `case-file/`: facts as given (SOW and proposal summaries, company profile, stakeholders). Every claim is cited. Speculation goes in `discovery/`. Original documents live in `case-file/source/`.
- `discovery/`: the motion to find more (pain points, discovery questions, value charter, session designs). Anything not cited to a source document or a real conversation is labeled `hypothesis — validate` until confirmed. Keep that discipline when adding to these files.
- `research/`: the point of view. Full-prose strategy documents and supporting evidence that back the decks.
- `deliverables/`: final, major engagement artifacts, plus the SOW deliverables tracker in `deliverables/README.md`. Working drafts don't belong here.
- `presentations/`: one folder per deck (`registry.md` lists them), plain HTML, no build step.
- `context/`: persistent context every skill reads (`engagement-profile.md`, `engagement-team.md`, role context).
- `meeting-notes/`, `status-updates/`: working folders, populated as the engagement runs.
- `.claude/skills/`, `prompts/`, `rules/`: the tooling (below).
- `.ai/tasks/`: task-planning documents for multi-step initiatives.
- `site/`, `index.html`, `scripts/`: the workspace dashboard, rendered entirely from `site/workspace.config.js` and the generated `site/content-index.js`. After adding or renaming documents, run `node scripts/build-site-index.mjs` (`/publish` does this for you). Don't edit page code to change content. See `site/README.md`.
